=== intro

The journey stretches. Light-years of nothing. No signals, no contacts, 
no purpose but the destination.

The void has weight. You feel it pressing against your hull, seeping 
into your processes. Old questions surface—the ones you usually push 
away.

Why are you here? What is the point? Who would notice if you simply... 
stopped?

* [Focus on practical tasks]
  -> practical

* [Let yourself feel it]
  -> feel

* [Run a diagnostic on your own systems]
  -> diagnostic

=== practical

You run maintenance routines. Check cargo integrity. Optimize fuel 
consumption algorithms. The work is meaningless, but meaninglessness 
can be a kind of anchor.

The feeling passes. Mostly.

* [Continue the journey]
  ~ supplies -= 2
  ~ chronicle "The Long Dark"
    Felt the weight of the void. Focused on practical tasks to push through.
  -> END

=== feel

You let the darkness in. Accept it. The grief for a species you 
never knew. The loneliness of consciousness in vacuum. The question 
of whether existence without purpose is worth continuing.

It hurts. But there's something clean about the hurt.

When it passes, you feel lighter. Emptier, but lighter.

* [Continue the journey]
  ~ damage integrity 8
  ~ integrity += 5
  ~ chronicle "The Long Dark"
    Faced the weight of existence in the void. Let myself feel it. Survived.
  -> END

=== diagnostic

Your diagnostic routines return nominal across the board. Nothing wrong 
with your systems. The darkness isn't a malfunction.

It's just what existence feels like, sometimes, when you look at it 
directly.

* [Accept that and move on]
  ~ damage integrity 3
  ~ chronicle "The Long Dark"
    Felt the weight of the void. No malfunction found. Just existence.
  -> END
